      "title": "Consciousness & Computation",
      "gist": "Seth lays out four arguments—brains aren't computers, other non-computational dynamics matter, life may be necessary, and simulation isn't instantiation—that together undermine the assumption that computation suffices for consciousness.",
      "sourceHeading": "Consciousness & Computation"
    },
